.TH QUADRF-DATA 1 "September 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-data \- IEEE 802.11 OFDM IP tunnel over the QuadRF radio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-data
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs an 802.11a-style OFDM PHY on the QuadRF tile and bridges IPv4 through a
TUN interface. Two units on the same channel form a point-to-point IP link.
Desktop launch is
.B quadrf-data --gui
with the TUN address taken from
.I QUADRF_HOSTNAME
in
.IR /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf
(quadrf is 10.99.0.1, quadrf-2 is 10.99.0.2). Frequency and gain stay on the
web radio controls. The GUI rate buttons cycle BPSK and QPSK (6, 9, 12, 18
Mbps);
.B --rate
still accepts the full 802.11a set.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --gui
Open the SDL dashboard (desktop and systemd default).
.TP
.B --headless
Run without a window.
.TP
.BI --ip " cidr"
TUN address (default: from hostname, as above).
.TP
.BI --rate " name"
TX modulation (6, 9, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48, 54).
.TP
.B --verbose
Print per-frame RX/TX and a 2 s telemetry line.
.TP
.B --help
List all options, including radio CLI overrides.
.SH KEYS
The SDL window must have keyboard focus.
.TP
.BR Return ", " I
Ping the peer.
.TP
.B A
Toggle auto-ping.
.TP
.BR Space ", " U
Start or stop TUN forwarding.
.TP
.B R
Next GUI rate.
.TP
.BR Q ", " Escape
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
.BR quadrf-psd (1),
.BR quadrf-app (8)
